      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T15:53:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Old habits die hard, I guess.  At the first job I had writing C code in 2001 the policy was that we could not be sure of the NULL macro across the various old Unix-flavors our code was supposed to run on, so we used integer zero, which according to some C standard implicitly converts to the null pointer.",
