      "lineNbr": 781,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T14:53:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should this use `STM32_GPIO_IDR(slot-\u003egpio_base) \u0026 slot-\u003egpio_pin_mask;` to be consistent?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 781,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "2aaf42d5945abcbeb15eea2b0d5a35df7ecd7f4c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "310345ce_ae7303b7",
        "filename": "board/hyperdebug/gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 781,
      "author": {
        "id": 1341996
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T15:53:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is a little odd to have one be uint32_t and the other be uint8_t.  However, using the same convention for `tail_level` will just make the C logic more complicated.  The reason I introduced the somewhat odd convention for `head_level`, is that it is used in the interrupt handler, and the next CL that introduces assembly code in the interrupt handler can take advantage of the convention, eliminating an instruction or two.",
      "parentUuid": "f7202244_2419487f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 781,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "2aaf42d5945abcbeb15eea2b0d5a35df7ecd7f4c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e8ad9ce_db3e882f",
        "filename": "board/hyperdebug/gpio.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 781,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-25T15:56:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I feel like we should make them consistent and have slightly more complex C code. I feel like it is asking for trouble in the future if we have two different styles of values.\n\nI don\u0027t know if reducing the asm by 2 instructions is worth it, but I will let you make that call. I think the smaller future maintenance cost is worth a few more lines of asm or C code.",
      "parentUuid": "310345ce_ae7303b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 781,
        "endChar": 46
      },
